\f0\fs22 \cf2 the experience of \'93searching\'94 is no longer physical. rather than moving through shelves in a library, we now surf through endless streams of information online. this project asks how the physicality of search might be restored within digital space.\
\
the website embeds wikipedia within an interface that records the user\'92s hand movements across the trackpad alongside the words they hover over while navigating information. at the end of each search session, the site generates a drawing that documents the movement of the search itself, tracing the gestures, pauses, and pathways through which knowledge was encountered. users can also \'93inspect\'94 the words they lingered over, revealing the duration and sequence of their attention.\
\
these collaborations between human cognition and computational systems are archived in a gallery on the homepage, reimagining what a search history could look like if it were treated as a material trace rather than invisible data. when hovering over a drawing in the archive, the associated words reappear sequentially, unfolding according to the amount of time spent on each one.\
\
the design of the landing section extends this idea of trace through a visual language derived from the arrangement of alphabets on a qwerty keyboard. a physical companion to the website takes the form of a booklet containing search sessions conducted over the course of a day, printed on semi-transparent vellum paper. its aspect ratio and rounded edges mirror those of a macbook trackpad.\
